this is one of hundreds of thousands of  Volkswagen vehicles in the united states  affected by the emissions scandal mark  hartman bought his VW golf from a dealer  in maryland last summer when his  daughter was born he wanted an  environmentally friendly and economical  family car but when he heard that VW  falsified its emission values he didn't  want to drive it anymore we saw that the  president of Volkswagen mr. Horne said  that it was going to take over a year to  fix all the cars I don't want to be  putting out that kind of pollution over  the next year I don't want my daughter  being exposed to that kind of thing over  the next year and honestly I just don't  trust Volkswagen anymore consumer  advocate Dan Becker heads an  environmental group that targets the  auto industry many VW customers have  sought his advice the consumers were  lied to by VW they need to be firm they  need to say what they want they can get  their vehicle fixed but it should be  completely fixed so it doesn't pollute  any more not just replace the software  for those consumers for whom that isn't  acceptable they should demand a full  refund at the original purchase price  and then they can go by a different car  that doesn't pollute so much from a  company that doesn't lie as much mark  hartman decided to fight for  compensation he had paid nearly thirty  thousand dollars for his golf and twice  asked for his money back from the dealer  in nearby Gaithersburg to no avail here  he set out to try again  I'd like to go in and and have a  conversation with them the been  disrespectful to me I don't feel like  they've told me the truth but you know  this is this is kind of a last  opportunity to to deal with this outside  of court we are not allowed to show the  dealer's angry reaction he threatened to  sue us and again mark Hardman got no  results after a few minutes he was sent  away and told to contact VW headquarters  I'm pretty cynical about how they would  treat me I mean I knew they wouldn't  take the car back they should it's the  right thing to do but but for them it's  about making money and for Volkswagen  it's about making money so now I have to  talk to a judge and get a judge to roll  in the case Hartman filed his lawsuit as  one of the first of hundreds of  compensation claims against VW US courts  will be occupied with the emissions  cheating scandal for some time to come
 

